  "body": "## [1.3.0] - 24.11.2026\n\n### Added\n- Add `is_crontab_user_sudo` parameter by @antoniorodr\n- Add is_crontab_user_sudo parameter by @antoniorodr\n- Add the new `is_crontab_user_sudo` where is needed by @antoniorodr\n- Add a better description for the crontab user input field by @antoniorodr\n- Add support for the SSH key path by @antoniorodr\n- Add SSH key path support by @antoniorodr\n- Add `_version.py` to gitignore by @antoniorodr\n\n### Changed\n- Bumps version to v1.3.0 by @antoniorodr\n- Use is_crontab_user_sudo when writing by @antoniorodr\n- Write is now using `is_crontab_user_sudo` by @antoniorodr\n- Refactor(connect): `connect_to_ssh_server` writes `ssh_key_path` to the by @antoniorodr\n- Create `is_user_sudo` and `ssh_key_path` helpers by @antoniorodr\n- Refactor find cronjob function by @antoniorodr\n- Update `get_version` by @antoniorodr\n- Import `_version.py` from init by @antoniorodr\n- Create hatch hook to update version by @antoniorodr\n\n### Fixed\n- Pass is_crontab_user_sudo where is necessary by @antoniorodr\n- Use `is_crontab_user_sudo` when showing/refreshing cronjobs by @antoniorodr\n- `write_remote_crontab` now uses `is_crontab_user_sudo` by @antoniorodr\n- Refresh the CronTable after switching servers by @antoniorodr\n- Fix duplicate connection by @antoniorodr\n- Update test_get_version by @antoniorodr\n\n### Removed\n- Remove unused parameters by @antoniorodr\n\n[1.3.0]: https://github.com/antoniorodr/cronboard/compare/v1.2.1...v1.3.0\n\n<!-- generated by git-cliff -->",
